## ✏️ My Contribution and Modifications

**Mahnoor Ahmer (63430)**

I added a time-based greeting** above the main `<h1>` heading in the Welcome section. It shows **Good Morning**, **Good Afternoon**, **Good Evening** or **Good Night** depending on the time of day, along with today's date.

Used a small **vanilla JavaScript** script (no libraries) Matched the existing style: white rounded pill, purple-to-pink gradient text, soft shadow and hover lift like the cards
Did not change any existing code; I only added new CSS, HTML and JS
- If JavaScript is turned off, it shows "👋 Welcome back!" so the layout never breaks

**Time ranges:**

| Time | Greeting |
|------|----------|
| 5:00 AM – 11:59 AM | 🌅 Good Morning! |
| 12:00 PM – 4:59 PM | ☀️ Good Afternoon! |
| 5:00 PM – 8:59 PM | 🌇 Good Evening! |
| 9:00 PM – 4:59 AM | 🌙 Good Night! |

### 1. CSS (added after `.welcome-text h1 span` in the `<style>` tag)

```css
/* Time-based greeting (added by Mahnoor) */
.greeting {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 10px;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  background: var(--white);
  padding: 8px 18px;
  border-radius: 50px;
  box-shadow: var(--shadow);
  margin-bottom: 18px;
  font-weight: 600;
  transition: transform 0.3s, box-shadow 0.3s;
}

.greeting:hover {
  transform: translateY(-3px);
  box-shadow: 0 14px 32px rgba(124, 58, 237, 0.2);
}

.greeting-text {
  background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--purple), var(--pink));
  -webkit-background-clip: text;
  background-clip: text;
  color: transparent;
}

.greeting-date {
  font-size: 14px;
  font-weight: 500;
  color: var(--text);
  padding-left: 10px;
  border-left: 2px solid #e2e8f0;
}
```

### 2. HTML (added above the `<h1>` inside `.welcome-text`)

```html
<!-- Time-based greeting (added by Mahnoor) -->
<div class="greeting">
  <span id="greeting-icon">👋</span>
  <span class="greeting-text" id="greeting-text">Welcome back!</span>
  <span class="greeting-date" id="greeting-date"></span>
</div>
```

### 3. JavaScript (added between `</footer>` and `</body>`)

```html
<!-- Time-based greeting script (added by Mahnoor) -->
<script>
  const now = new Date();
  const hour = now.getHours();

  let greeting, icon;

  if (hour >= 5 && hour < 12) {
    greeting = "Good Morning!";
    icon = "🌅";
  } else if (hour >= 12 && hour < 17) {
    greeting = "Good Afternoon!";
    icon = "☀️";
  } else if (hour >= 17 && hour < 21) {
    greeting = "Good Evening!";
    icon = "🌇";
  } else {
    greeting = "Good Night!";
    icon = "🌙";
  }

  const today = now.toLocaleDateString("en-GB", {
    weekday: "long",
    day: "numeric",
    month: "long",
    year: "numeric"
  });

  document.getElementById("greeting-text").textContent = greeting;
  document.getElementById("greeting-icon").textContent = icon;
  document.getElementById("greeting-date").textContent = "📅 " + today;
</script>
```

